      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The study enrolled 30 patients aged 2 to 18 years, who had been operated on at the Prof A. L. Polenov Russian Neurosurgical Institute in 2008-2009. The patients had undergone total intravenous anesthesia with the opioid analgesic fentanyl (3.5 microg/kg x hr), the central alpha 2-adrenoblocker clofelin (1.2 microg/kg x hr), recofol (3 mg/kg x hr) under myorelaxation (arduan, esmeron) and artificial ventilation. Assessment of a neuroendocrine response and postoperative analgesia levels by the physiological and self-appraisal scales showed the high efficacy of pre-emptive analgesia using paracetamol in the complex of multicomponent anesthesia using the central alpha 2-adrenoblocker clofelin."},
